# Command to the mission control backend (arm_mission mission_control_node.py, /mission_control/command), defined here like PresetCommand: the rviz panel
# (MissionPanel) and the rqt plugin are its clients.
#   action  "refresh"       snapshot the plants in view (nearest to the gripper axis first), select #0 and make it the grasp target
#           "select"        make plant `index` of the snapshot the grasp target
#           "set_approach"  `text`: down | forward | an angle below the horizontal in degrees (45)
#           "set_bias"      `values` = [radial, tangential, vertical] metres, the aim bias in the arm frame
#           "set_height"    `values` = [metres]: the pinch point above the floor (the plant list must be refreshed afterwards)
#           "dry_run"       plan the grasp of the current settings; nothing moves
#           "go"            the real grasp; refused unless a dry run of EXACTLY the current settings succeeded recently
#           "stop"          stop the running grasp (always accepted)
# Everything except stop is refused while a grasp is running.
string action
int32 index
float64[] values
string text
---
bool success
string message
